// Stage 9's tests: the stock widgets of basic.ctx and slider.ctx, the two themes and the marks.
//
//  - Goldens (golden/basic-*.txt) of each widget at rest, hovered, pressed, focused and disabled,
//    in both themes; of the widgets that take no input at rest and disabled; of a tooltip; of every
//    widget at scale 1.5; and a node snapshot.
//  - Properties: no mark is text; at scale 1.5 every border is the same number of pixels on all
//    four sides and the boxes are the sizes the conversion rules give their lengths; a scene of
//    every widget recorded at eight positions a pixel apart draws the same shapes moved by exactly
//    the offset.
//  - Scripted: a click flips a checkbox and Space does too; a drag moves a slider by its share of
//    the track and onto its step, the keys step it; Enter and Space work a focused button, which
//    Tab gives focus to; a radio button takes its choice; the hand cursor over what can be used.
//
// How the goldens' numbers come about, at scale 1 in the tests' font at the themes' 14 units (a
// character 7 pixels wide, a line 14 high): a button is 28 high, padded 12 across, its label
// centred (7 above, 7 below); a checkbox's box is 16 square, 6 before its label, centred in a row
// 28 high (6 above); a slider's track is 4 high centred in 28, its knob 16 square centred on it.
// The scenes stand at (10, 10) in a column 216 wide, so a slider's track is 200 long.

#test
fn draws_a_button_in_its_six_looks_in_the_dark_theme { mut t: Test, mut io: Io, mut fs: Fs, mut mem: Mem } -> ! {
    let mut heap = ui_check::make_heap{ &mem }
    let dump = try make_dump{ &heap }
    try record_states{ &io, &fs, &t, &heap, out = dump.out, scratch = dump.scratch, widget = Widget::button, dark = true, name = "button", theme = "dark" }
}

